ms","html_url":"https://github.com/alabsystems","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":1115182,"digest":"sha256:501e9a57d6ee64fa87de7c56e26ebf45eb415915097acf672c4306852670448a","download_count":1,"created_at":"2026-10-20T08:40:39Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T08:40:39Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/alabsystems/aterm/releases/download/v0.107.0/SHA256SUMS"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alabsystems/aterm/releases/assets/658756269","id":658756269,"node_id":"RA_kwDOTfvfa84nQ9Kt","name":"SHA256SUMS.sig","label":"","uploader":{"login":"alabsystems","id":306342282,"node_id":"U_kgDOEkJpig","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/306342282?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems","html_url":"https://github.com/alabsystems","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alabsystems/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":64,"digest":"sha256:9e90597d3bc328a4d30e453f1163bae98fbd477d70543c8be2305579837ecebc","download_count":1,"created_at":"2026-10-20T08:40:40Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T08:40:41Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/alabsystems/aterm/releases/download/v0.107.0/SHA256SUMS.sig"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alabsystems/aterm/tarball/v0.107.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/alabsystems/aterm/zipball/v0.107.0","body":"# aterm v0.107.0\\n\\n2026-10-20 · 2074 changes since v0.106.0\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n- **keeper:** a RELEASE the keeper dropped unread is told again until a SYNC answers behind it\\n- **harness-card:** the rainbow prints vivid on a light theme\\n- **harness:** DECIDED FOR YOU — the choices the harness made in the person's name today (§10.4, slice 3)\\n- **autopilot:** the pause told — a short-turn back-off reads \\"pausing until 18:41\\" (design §10.5 slice 4a)\\n- **autopilot:** the A/B book by word and cause — boxes and questions compared, not idle time (design §10.5 slice 4b)\\n- **autopilot:** the A/B book kept for seven days, one file per process (design §10.5 slice 4c)\\n- **windows:** overlay scrollbar, hairline split seams, hollow pane cursors\\n- **windows:** jump list Recent directories and a taskbar bell badge\\n- **windows:** ship a pinned, signed OpenConsole.exe beside aterm\\n- **windows:** the bundled OpenConsole is the default console host\\n- **aterm-lab:** the crash verb, and LAB\\\\_INSTANCE\\\\_ENV recorded for the lab's own instance\\n- **agy, gui, effects:** agy launch card, composer harness rule, markdown glass & multi-line rainbow wrap\\n- **agent, ctl, gui:** fleet accounts CSV/LAN sync, dashboard, and limit account introspection\\n- **phase, agent, gui:** unified ALab kitty border-and-banner branding, single harness toggle, and visual markdown hierarchy for claude, agy, and muse\\n- **gui:** Autopilot v4 slice 6 — the verdict up front, and the ends counted\\n- **gui:** Settings ▸ Harness's Every session row (Autopilot v4, slice 5)\\n\\n## Fixes\\n\\n- **keeper:** a quit whose BYE was lost owes its returned offers nothing, so it relaunches nothing\\n- **keeper:** a stale RELEASE read late from an older link never ends a newer link's claim\\n- **harness-card:** tippy's cloned\\\\_ref\\\\_to\\\\_slice\\\\_refs in the vividness test; doc wording\\n- **harness:** DECIDED FOR YOU says what was decided, in the run it was decided in (§10.4 review)\\n- **autopilot:** the A/B book splits every session's stretch at midnight; review fixes on 4a-4c\\n- **autopilot:** the A/B book's charge never loops on a midnight that would not move on\\n- **autopilot:** a read title rebuilt by main's TitleReading::refresh keeps the pause as a stamp\\n- **harness:** a limit's end answers a plain question or stop as continue@v1 does\\n- **harness:** a 403 authentication\\\\_failed notice is the lost login, not a refused request\\n- **harness:** an image or attachment full context is told the way back its notice names\\n- **harness:** a notice behind a prompt command right after an error notice is read again\\n- **harness:** an answer typed at a limit's end under any question priority is the limit's try\\n- **harness:** a limit episode closes where the policy reads the limit over, busy read or not\\n- **harness:** a countdown whose notice was written before the agent started goes on by nobody\\n- **harness:** at a limit's reset, another conversation's words get the continue policy's act\\n- **harness:** behind a background shell, another conversation's done report gets no keep going at a limit's reset\\n- **harness:** the vendor's word that it went on, read before the limit's reset, is another day's\\n- **harness:** a conversation's move outlives the record that carried it\\n- **harness:** a relaunch's first decision reads the limit its transcript stands at\\n- **harness:** a bucket's notice older than the relaunched process is the one the fallback left\\n- **phase:** a generic countdown row under a model's bucket is the bucket's\\n- **harness:** a bare `API Error: 403 …` whose login failed is the lost login\\n- **harness:** a turn seen running asks the transcript whether a limit stands\\n- **harness:** `aterm drive watch|supervise` read the tab's Claude Code's record\\n- **harness:** a done report said as a condition is none; `already completed` after the task's subject is one\\n- **harness:** the token first over open work at the done check gets the challenge, not the end\\n- **harness:** a conversation only a peer directed has a task\\n- **harness:** the record reads a wall's retry by its ledger rule, not by the words alone\\n- **harness:** a release typed at a break of background work is a carry-on, as at an idle point\\n- **upgrade:** the upgrade\\\\_ask look reads a token behind long wakes (ATERM-KI-1016-1)\\n- **turn-end:** a loop that follows an older build's ledger knows the job was challenged (ATERM-KI-1016-1)\\n- **upgrade:** Land's answer after the instruction is Land's check to the record (ATERM-KI-1016-1)\\n- **turn-end:** the vendor's own continuation delivers the check a limit cut again (ATERM-KI-1016-1)\\n- **upgrade:** a /loop wake on a build that numbers no turn is a turn of its own (ATERM-KI-1016-1)\\n- **relaunch:** the hand-run sweep's carry-on reads the tab's own Autopilot (ATERM-KI-1016-1)\\n- **upgrade:** a restart's finished read reaches back past a window that settles nothing (ATERM-KI-1016-1)\\n- **turn-end:** a done phrase led by any subordinator is no done report (ATERM-KI-1016-1, KR-DONE-1)\\n- **turn-end:** a subject that names part of the task is no done report (ATERM-KI-1016-1, KR-DONE-2)\\n- **upgrade:** a missed task's notice is a turn of its own with no promptId (ATERM-KI-1016-1, KR-DONE-4)\\n- **upgrade:** one carry-on reads the record once, and the look's memo is pinned (ATERM-KI-1016-1, KR-DONE-3)\\n- **codex:** a relaunched Codex reads Land and its redrawn last reply before its carry-on (ATERM-KI-1016-1, KR-DONE-5)\\n- **turn-end:** the switch's reset types no carry-on into a done task (ATERM-KI-1016-1, KR-DONE-5)\\n- **turn-end:** the switch's own steps neither reopen nor hold a done task (ATERM-KI-1016-1, KR-DONE-5)\\n- **harness:** a loop that follows reads the end of a turn the loop before read running as a turn that ran (ATERM-KI-1016-1, follow-4)\\n- **harness:** a loop that follows takes up an API error's retry ladder (ATERM-KI-1016-1, follow-3)\\n- **harness:** a loop that follows counts a no-reset limit's first rung from the wall (ATERM-KI-1016-1, follow-1)\\n- **harness:** the ledger's cut keeps the rows of states that stand for days, records not counted (ATERM-KI-1016-1, follow-6)\\n- **harness:** a loop that follows reads its own first look as an unread try's first read, however late (ATERM-KI-1016-1, follow-2)\\n- **harness:** the first loop after an older build's reads where that loop stood from its journal (ATERM-KI-1016-1, follow-5)\\n- **harness:** a loop in a tab a cold restore reopened takes up the books of the tab it was reopened from (ATERM-KI-1016-1, follow-7)\\n- **harness:** the ledger's cut reads its files in harness::cli again, as the supervise-fx guard asks (ATERM-KI-1016-1, follow-6, follow-7)\\n- **harness:** a second cold restore reads the earlier books only as far as the tab between still carries them (ATERM-KI-1016-1, follow-7, KRF-3)\\n- **harness:** the ledger's cut keeps only the rows that move a standing state, so it stays bounded while Land or a switch stands (ATERM-KI-1016-1, follow-6, KRF-2)\\n- **harness:** a person's exchange left to them is keyed by its prompt (ATERM-KI-1016-1, person-5)\\n- **harness:** the live upgrade asks nothing at a person's own exchange (ATERM-KI-1016-1, person-8)\\n- **harness:** a wall's retry keeps a person's exchange at the wall open (ATERM-KI-1016-1, person-7)\\n- **harness:** a loop that follows leaves a person's exchange as the loop before it (ATERM-KI-1016-1, person-6)\\n- **harness:** an Esc on the act's answer ends a follower's carry too (ATERM-KI-1016-1, person-6, review KR-P6-ESC)\\n- **harness:** a command the agent does not answer is no turn of its own (ATERM-KI-1016-1, person-5, review KR-P5-CMD)\\n- **harness:** an owed release's settle owns its point (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-2)\\n- **supervise:** a move repeated at an unchanged point spends a follow-up (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-3)\\n- **harness:** one unreadable upgrade record keeps its last row, not the whole view (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-8)\\n- **harness:** the window keeps a tab whose upgrade record cannot be read (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-8)\\n- **harness:** a carried restart that did not land is said as its record's agent (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-6)\\n- **harness:** a restored end is decided before its tab's word is cleared (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-4)\\n- **harness:** the window words the restored agents' row from what the host said (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-7)\\n- **harness:** a restored step that panicked reads its record before it is said (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-5)\\n- **harness:** one tab's part of a host pass that panics is that tab's alone (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-1)\\n- **harness:** the owner is told when the upgrades' records cannot be listed (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-8)\\n- **harness:** a typed relaunch line is recorded before the ledger line (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-5)\\n- **harness:** a tab's stage that panicked is asked again on the host's back-off (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-1, KR-HOST-1)\\n- **harness:** a restored landing that is only its record in flight is said at the fault budget (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-5, KR-HOST-3)\\n- **harness:** a restored landing's end asks no hook once its attempt is off the queue (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-4, KR-HOST-6)\\n- **harness:** a restored row nobody saw through comes back inside the next (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-7, KR-HOST-4)\\n- **harness:** an upgrade record this look cannot read leaves its tab exactly as it stands (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-8, KR-HOST-2)\\n- **harness:** an unreadable upgrade record keeps its conversation's tab and is said to the owner (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-8, KR-HOST-5)\\n- **harness:** a tab stage's rung that has passed wakes the host for nothing (ATERM-KI-1016-1 host-1)\\n- **phase:** a rating card whose first box Ink wraps is still the card (ATERM-KI-1016-1 dialogs: rating cards)\\n- **phase:** a Select label Ink wraps at a name or inside a word reads whole (ATERM-KI-1016-1 dialogs: held message, Computer Use, usage-limit dialog)\\n- **phase:** a button row with the text's residue glued to it is no button (ATERM-KI-1016-1 Questions: the one-word residue)\\n- **harness:** a question the loop's Enter answered, asked again with no read between, is a new dialog (ATERM-KI-1016-1 Questions: the gap no read samples)\\n- **harness:** a draft over a slash menu that marks its entry in colour only is sent only onto its own command (KR-DLG-2, ATERM-KI-1016-1 dialogs: no pointer)\\n- **harness:** a box taller than the pane is answered whole from its head in the main screen's history (KR-DLG-1, ATERM-KI-1016-1 dialogs: a box whose head is off the screen)\\n- **restore:** a held tab's agent the owner's lift left with no hold is named on no leaf inside the drain\\n- **crash-journal:** a word's OK is a durability ack, and an image the writer could not publish is owed again\\n- **crash-journal:** an agent publication owes the journal a capture now, not at the write interval\\n- **harness:** the record a crash left is what the layout names through the relaunch's back-off\\n- **harness:** the worker's own readers follow the agent's record before they read the kept copy\\n- **harness:** a layout's read of an agent's record holds the window's loop one bound at most\\n- **crash-journal:** a capture activity prompted owes one trailing settle at the interval's end\\n- **restore:** Windows' end-session snapshot takes a word about typing at once, and carries the holds\\n- **control:** only the owner's slot waits on the crash journal; the fleet's holds are answered at once\\n- **restore:** a held tab lifted inside the cold drain says its agent's record at the lift\\n- **restore:** a held tab lifted on aterm's last turn is said before the message log closes\\n- **relaunch:** a moved agent's finish is found without the host's note (ATERM-KI-1016-1)\\n- **relaunch:** unset login under another home is that home's login (ATERM-KI-1016-1)\\n- **aterm-lab:** `ps <tag>` and `down <tag>` act on that tag when its lab is down (ATERM-KI-1016-1)\\n- **aterm-lab:** `restore --codex` judges the relaunch's continuation (ATERM-KI-1016-1)\\n- **upgrade:** an afresh move's row takes a word and names its mark's command (ATERM-KI-1016-1)\\n- **upgrade:** the first move onto a never-run build is probed before it ends an agent (ATERM-KI-1016-1)\\n- **upgrade-view:** an agent-down row the owner answered stays answered across an aterm restart (ATERM-KI-1016-1)\\n- **upgrade:** the build-start probe's test seam is the tests' alone (ATERM-KI-1016-1, relaunch-3)\\n- **harness:** a lost word crosses a seamless update with its tab (ATERM-KI-1016-1, relaunch-1 LC-4)\\n- **handoff:** the person's stamp crosses a seamless update (ATERM-KI-1016-1, relaunch-1 LC-4)\\n- **restore:** the leaf's lost word is boxed, the view's size lint allowed as the tree's (ATERM-KI-1016-1, relaunch-1 LC-4)\\n- **aterm-lab:** `restore --codex`'s verdict is one pure function its run returns (ATERM-KI-1016-1, relaunch-11)\\n- **handoff:** the successor's Commit takes the supervision over in one step its tests run (ATERM-KI-1016-1, relaunch-1 LC-4)\\n- **harness:** a never-keyed shell says since when, so a relaunch through a hand is typed at its lift (ATERM-KI-1016-1, relaunch-1 LC-4)\\n- **relaunch:** a sweep types a restore look's line where the tab's own Autopilot is on (ATERM-KI-1016-1, relaunch-6)\\n- **upgrade:** a fresh shell-gone row is answered by the new tab's Claude Code (relaunch-4, KR-7)\\n- **harness:** the drive directory keeps the session journal's budget (relaunch-10, KR-5)\\n- **harness:** the upgrade ledger links a tab to the tabs it held a conversation in (relaunch-7, KR-4)\\n- **gui:** name the Commit's host-resume probe type (tippy type\\\\_complexity, relaunch-1 KR-1)\\n- **upgrade:** a move onto a build that fails only at a real start is taken back onto the build the agent ran (LC-5, ATERM-KI-1016-1)\\n- **harness:** a draft over an older Claude Code's `@` menu is sent only with no entry selected (ATERM-KI-1016-1, dialogs: no pointer)\\n- **aterm-lab:** a wait on a child the kernel will not watch waits until it is reaped\\n- **windows:** aterm-uds's ownerlock module exists on every platform\\n- **windows:** atpkg on Windows: gc reads the process table, ALab entrypoints stay in their package\\n- **windows:** Windows TLS verification requires a subjectAltName match\\n- **windows:** the Trust toolchain is found on Windows; small crates' tests run there\\n- **windows:** the harness, supervise and ai review work on Windows\\n- **windows:** colour emoji on Windows, fitted to their cells\\n- **windows:** local time, path links and video retention work in aterm-gui on Windows\\n- **windows:** aterm-agent's Windows tests pass, its flakes wait on events, two Windows bugs fixed\\n- **windows:** directory pins share delete like a Unix descriptor\\n- **windows:** whole colour emoji, letter flags, spinner stars, CJK weight\\n- **windows:** legible theme colours: contrast floor, blues, COLORFGBG\\n- **windows:** shells report the right exit code and line; Ctrl+J runs it\\n- **windows:** layouts, dead keys, Alt codes; PSReadLine keeps its chords\\n- **windows:** aterm's own icon, sharp at every size, and an aterm class\\n- **windows:** close-all asks every window; windows open placed and themed\\n- **windows:** caption, tab band and Settings as one surface in your accent\\n- **windows:** pane-scoped find bar, F3, Fluent palette and switches\\n- **appearance:** light Settings cards rise above the page on Windows only\\n- **windows:** COLORFGBG names the side of the theme the tab will draw\\n- **core:** theme floor caps only page text under SGR 7 and DECSCNM\\n- **windows:** a theme replace also retries a sharing or lock violation\\n- **windows:** pwsh: a parse error reads 1, a repeated native code holds\\n- **windows:** a held key after an uncomposed dead key repeats alone\\n- **linux:** Linux keeps its tab strip look; the new one is Windows-only\\n- **windows:** captures and recordings of a minimized window still present\\n- **windows:** a window re-asserts its menu side as it activates\\n- **windows:** a split's find panel lays no rail that lifts its sibling\\n- **windows:** the palette scrim is its own layer and lifts for themes\\n- **windows:** aterm-gui builds on Windows with no warnings again\\n- **windows:** elevated aterm holds its control socket to Administrators\\n- **windows:** OpenConsole leaves a killed pager's alternate screen\\n- **windows:** keep OpenConsole's five arguments and kitty keys off\\n- **windows:** Git Bash keeps every key after a resize in OpenConsole\\n- **windows:** OpenConsole's health check blames only the host, and a GUI program runs once\\n- **windows:** aterm.exe, not cmd.exe, leaves a dead app's alternate screen and keeps the console input mode\\n- **terminal:** the console host's switch out of a dead app's screen releases the app's modes\\n- **ctl:** mainscreen says ERR timeout when the console host does not leave\\n- **windows:** a program left by an earlier tab no longer counts as running in a new one\\n- **windows:** main's worker tasks, survey and spawn line read Windows paths\\n- **windows:** gate the Unix-only fleet, bye and handoff-carry items so aterm-gui and aterm-net build warning-free\\n- **windows:** refuse xterm modifyOtherKeys behind a console host, as kitty is\\n- **windows:** a killed full-screen app's bracketed paste and size reports end at the next prompt\\n- **windows:** KP\\\\_Begin, F13-F20 and the DECKPAM keypad reach console programs under OpenConsole\\n- **windows:** Alt+U, Alt+L and Alt+C change a word's case in Windows PowerShell 5.1\\n- **windows:** terminal replies pass the ConPTY resize guard, so a window drag no longer types into Git Bash\\n- **windows:** the host's alternate-screen leave also turns off in-band size and colour-scheme reports\\n- **windows:** the split divider shows which pane has focus, and its scrollbar sits on the line\\n- **windows:** the tab strip draws Windows 11 tabs, with air under its rule\\n- **windows:** Git Bash tabs read their home as \\\\~\\n- **windows:** Settings' resting controls rise above their cards on light themes\\n- **windows:** Settings' colour preview draws its title bar the way the window will\\n- **windows:** the command palette opens on a search box, selects like Settings, and keeps grey for disabled commands\\n- **windows:** find keeps its toggles in a split, gains ↑ ↓ ✕, and its current match reads at full strength\\n- **windows:** the app folder and install carry every licence text NOTICE cites\\n- **windows:** a tab's shell integration follows the program it runs\\n- `aterm ctl settings set|unset` names a key written by hand\\n- **windows:** the keypad stays key records in keypad application mode under both console hosts\\n- **windows:** a size report a pwsh command turns on is no longer typed into its next line\\n- **windows:** the pwsh prompt on a killed app's screen comes along when the console host leaves it\\n- closing the palette or a card replays no pointer the window has lost\\n- **windows:** the selected tab joins what lies under it, sizes to its title and draws its emoji\\n- **windows:** the divider between two 