A ruling R5, design §7.4)\\n- **machines:** the LAN daemon answers a beacon and nothing else; launchd no longer loops on it\\n- **machines:** no LAN daemon; follow a moved IP to its .local name, retire the old LaunchAgent\\n- **aterm-window:** recorded.rs as its crate's rustfmt.toml formats it\\n- **machines:** retiring the old LaunchAgent takes only what the job made, and starts nothing\\n- **trust:** bump vendor/astream and eliminate 60 unproved obligations across 9 crates (+96 proved)\\n- docs+test(supervise): a transcript limit row that names no reset holds the host's steps until the conversation moves (ATERM-KI-1016-1 limits-2)\\n- docs+test(supervise): a restart's lease refuses the supervisor's limit-menu press too, retried (ATERM-KI-1016-1 limits-4)\\n- docs+test(supervise): a bucket notice nothing dates is read by the fallback's latch alone (ATERM-KI-1016-1 limits-6)\\n- docs+test(manual): a person's prompt moves a limit row's hold only once the model answers it (ATERM-KI-1016-1 limits-2)\\n- turn end: a draft over a menu the screen cannot read is told once, never pressed (screens-2)\\n- **approval:** the Edit tool's own box is the levels' where the screen and the transcript both name its call (screens-3)\\n- box head: a box taller than the pane is held, the owner told, wherever its head is not read whole within 400 rows (screens-1)\\n- **approval:** the Edit tool's box is its message's queued run's top, past the agent's text (screens-3 review)\\n- **manual:** the boxes paragraph's tall-box sentence rewrapped to the page (screens-1 review)\\n- **decide(harness):** an agent the upgrade ended is said down in a tab Off set aside (lifecycle-1)\\n- **decide(harness):** a driver's writes under its lease are no person's keys; what it left holds the line (lifecycle-2, LC-7)\\n- **decide(restore):** a held tab reopens held, its agent the holder's; a lift no image carries comes back (lifecycle-3, LC-8)\\n- **manual:** two lines the done and limits lanes added rewrapped to their paragraphs' width\\n- **aterm-gui:** session 0's shell is forked before the event loop is built\\n- **aterm-shell-integration:** the script folder is named with FxHasher, not FNV-1a/64\\n- **aterm-gui:** session\\\\_log's attribution tests are unix tests, as their handles are\\n- **aterm-update-core:** a silently dead download is given up in \\\\~14 s and continued in-call\\n- **aterm-update-core:** a link that keeps moving is continued past sixteen hiccups; bytes already at download\\\\_to's dest are never continued\\n- **aterm-update-core:** a resumable attempt probes an idle connection every 2 s, not 5\\n- **atpkg:** a release row naming the dmg lane is refused as an https one is\\n- **atpkg:** the dmg lane's post-copy vet refusal is tested through the stage\\n- **aterm-agent:** a probe run counts a hundred steps, not three hundred\\n- LAG-11 review: say why the script folder may persist an FxHasher name, and quote the idle band\\n- **LAG-12:** no work interval for the idle slow clock (warm-spare design D6)\\n- **spare:** fish tabs get their warm spare back over the startup roots fish reports (R7)\\n- **spare:** the generation stamps path\\\\_helper's PATH list and fish's themes folder\\n- **vendor(astream):** advance submodule to 72a46fb (+702 proved / -74 unknown in astream, unlock BrokerLog on drop)\\n- **LAG-12:** D6 carries the four-round result: the interval made the shell's first prompt later\\n- LAG-12 review: D6 measured in aterm.app's own coalition too\\n- **aterm-gui:** a stream that stalls under a frame keeps its output holds\\n- **aterm-gui:** say why a stream's quiet window is one frame, and whose 0.38 ms\\n- **grid:** a shrink under owed pushed rows pushes the blank row a push left, never trims it (S2R-F4 corner b)\\n- **grid:** a width change lays the rows out where the hand-back puts them (S2R-F4 corner a)\\n- cast drift: each recording replays under the resize law its header names (S2R-F4 corner c)\\n- **aterm-slog:** the instance's node log (5J-1)\\n- aterm-gui, aterm-gui-fabric: start, link and config records (5J-2)\\n- aterm-gui, aterm-types: log n reads the node log (5J-3)\\n- **aterm-gui:** await log takes a list of predicates (5F-1)\\n- aterm-agent, aterm-gui: the hosted lanes say they relaunched (5F-2)\\n- **aterm-slog:** a turn's close restates its ledger= (5F-4a)\\n- **aterm-agent:** drive ledger --source log, beside the old path (5F-4)\\n- **aterm-ctl:** survey --brief, the local brief (5F-6)\\n- **aterm-ctl:** the survey walk dials one instance at a time (5F-6)\\n- **aterm-lab:** lab reduce, a key-only reducer (5H-1)\\n- **aterm-agent:** measured builds are a committed set (5H-2a)\\n- **aterm-agent:** a lab-read reduction makes its build exact (5H-2b)\\n- **aterm-gui:** the transcript apply's hold is a metric (5H-3)\\n- **aterm-gui:** a read with no new rows books its one hold (5H-3)\\n- **aterm-lab:** format the reducer's dead-code expectation (5H-1)\\n- **aterm-ctl:** a since-less await log list is asked again only when all need (5F-1)\\n- **aterm-ctl:** survey --brief briefs an instance that refuses log n (5F-6)\\n- **aterm-agent:** drive ledger --source log names a turn no exchange opened (5F-4)\\n- **aterm-lab:** lab reduce keeps no key or stamp tail anyone wrote (5H-1)\\n- **aterm-lab:** lab reduce frees every place a tool's names sit (5H-1)\\n- **aterm-lab:** lab reduce frees a call's second input copy and every tool schema (5H-1)\\n- aterm-core SPECS: the flap identity holds through the bottom-push and rewrap corners\\n- cast drift: name the law test's corner tuple (tippy type\\\\_complexity)\\n- **shell-integration:** an in-place upgrade takes off the old \\\\~/.aterm/bin entry\\n- **codesign:** a dangling symlink and a later-line fault stay verdicts\\n- **update:** codesign's own progress lines and a quoted refusal key never make a verdict pass (r8 #37, review)\\n- **aterm-update:** no decision reads floor/failed/quarantine ledgers permissively\\n- **update:** judge the appcast sig after the roster observation; one filing per stage state across the park\\n- **update:** a codesign refusal is a moment only on the verified path's own line; ditto's words are quoted (r8 #37, third review)\\n- **update:** gates read quarantine records strictly; codesign never waits on a FIFO; test the yank and authority call sites\\n- **trust:** raise aterm-agent's floor to 4509/25102 and correct aterm-cli's total to 1005\\n- **aterm-gui:** Settings' rail grows to its widest name in the face it is drawn in\\n- **aterm-gui:** crash-journal tests date their panic reports after the run armed\\n- Linux lane: web2, the worktree's git, Trust's absence and Rosetta's limits decided\\n- aterm-objc tests: the SDK declaration parser passes over a `pub const fn`\\n- **aterm-gui:** the rail test judges 1.25x, where full names overran it first\\n- **vendor(astream):** bump to 4db9781 (+229 proved / -194 unknown obligations in astream-broker)\\n- resize hand-back: a line's head comes onto the screen before a width change; pushes cut seams, never splice\\n- resize hand-back: the window's top is a cell, so a zoom flap over a line the screen's top cuts comes back\\n- **update:** the day-long digest line names no platform (ATERM-KI-1015-2)\\n- **manual:** Linux update checks wait while a build is on trial, as the product's rule (ATERM-KI-1015-2)\\n- **input:** an xkb chord under Caps Lock takes Shift's capital (ATERM-KI-1015-9, the X11/Wayland case)\\n- **style(gui):** trustfmt the xkb chord test and the fork-lane descriptor test\\n- The parent installs an update before LaunchServices launches its successor, so that successor never re-execs\\n- Review fixes for the parent-swaps-first handoff: withdraw a dead successor's stale-record entry, and correct the lane prose\\n- A fresh window ends the stale-record entry, and the last premises say who swaps\\n- Every window measures its own LaunchServices record and says when it is stale\\n- **spec(gui):** mh-health-latch-heal names the queued owed row's patience restart (ATERM-KI-1015-2, U37 review)\\n- **aterm-gui:** the toolbar drive's state count is the groups' own\\n- **aterm-gui:** objc\\\\_ime\\\\_drive's Option-as-Alt stage gets a control that composes\\n- **aterm-gui:** the toolbar drive reads a click made without activation as not measured\\n- **aterm-verify:** the objc exit contract names both weaker passes and the toolbar's activation 2\\n- **aterm-gui:** objc\\\\_ime\\\\_drive judges only the key it sends\\n- **aterm-window:** replace\\\\_event's doc cites the dead-key measurement\\n- **primer:** drop ATERM-TASK-DONE from the CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md section (v28)\\n- harness card: a cuter kitty, and the rainbow meets its haunch\\n- harness card: the border stands in the card's air\\n- **claude\\\\_footer:** read a new Claude Code's registry row on a 100 ms ladder, so the harness card is decorated at load\\n- harness card: the resolver's pass is tested as run calls it, the two-row kitty's mouth stands on its chin, and the docs say what was measured\\n- **claude\\\\_card:** the air comment names agy's four-row card\\n- **aterm-gui:** main builds again after …\\n- aterm-core, aterm-render, aterm-gpu: tippy passes again after …\\n- aterm-lab, aterm-agent: the lab's Codex 0.163.0 rollouts, reduced (5G lab run; T9, T33)\\n- **aterm-phase:** Codex's rollout keys, from a committed rollout (5G-1; T9)\\n- **aterm-agent:** a Codex rollout step fold (5G-2; T9, T33, S6)\\n- A macOS window launch keeps its image and leaves a ready update for its own window\\n- Window launch keeps its image: press-only never escapes, one boot router, waits said true\\n- Window launch keeps its image: the bar waits for a terminal too, recheck fixes\\n- Recheck lab instance custody after crash preparation waits\\n- Preserve post-shell PATH directories with backdated modification times\\n- **aterm-gui:** the warm spare on Linux, both tiers, with a /proc escape scan\\n- **aterm-gui:** the Linux scan's tick rate reads c\\\\_ulong as the codebase does on LP64\\n- **aterm-gui:** the Linux scan declares getauxval itself, so x86\\\\_64 Linux builds\\n- **aterm\\\\_suite:** the turn-submit stand-in draws its draft when the Enter comes with it\\n- **aterm-gui:** the Linux scan judges a live thread group whose leader exited, and a parked spawn looks for the system files again\\n- **aterm-gui:** rewrap the /proc stat parser's doc comment\\n- Share the argv0 alias list and deny the amacs editor hint per hop\\n- Name build.ps1's prose alias lists and drop a repeated EDITOR assert\\n- Harden account source curl configuration and protocols\\n- Preserve unknown Linux proc reads before warm promotion\\n\\n_Truncated to fit GitHub's release-body limit — the complete note is `release-notes/v0.107.0.md` in this release's source tree._\\n\\n---\\n\\nSource release. `SHA256SUMS` is a per-file manifest of the released tree, with a detached Ed25519 signature (`SHA256SUMS.sig`) by a machine key named in the attached master-signed roster (`aterm-machines.toml` + `.sig`). Verification chain and key inventory: SIGNING.md in the publication engine; the roster pin is committed in aterm `crates/aterm-update-core/src/pins.rs`.\\n"}
