ace Kitty encoding, Ctrl-R/S composer cursor snap, and trail revive/ring fixes\\n- **recovery:** refuse multiply named journal images\\n- **release:** keep raw proof reports after reduction fails\\n- **settings:** a landing stands until a render has seated it (post-check behaviour-2, owner-eye-2)\\n- **settings:** the landed SESSIONS row's card holds its whole block, clear of its words (post-check owner-eye-3)\\n- **harness:** one name for each count on Settings ▸ Harness, and unproven said once (post-check owner-eye-6)\\n- **harness:** STATUS's today notes in the page's plain type, Hero only for counts (post-check owner-eye-7)\\n- **autopilot:** the menu says its session's whole name and stays in its pane (post-check behaviour-3)\\n- **harness:** a note keeps the counts' room, so nothing under STATUS moves when they come\\n- **settings:** every open of Settings ▸ Harness replaces the landing before it, the top too\\n- **autopilot:** the menu keeps to its pane's rows too, and gives a tight pane its words first\\n- **autopilot:** a card neither side of its chip holds covers the chip's row, whole\\n- **input, update:** one busy answer for a full input queue; the Commit never cuts an owed input reply\\n- **update:** the cold lane's exec waits for a closed tab's shell reap\\n- **kitty:** consume a t=t file or t=s object only once the engine took it\\n- **control:** background input on the ordered writer's route answers from the write\\n- **pty, sink:** Stop paste and a tab's close release a writer blocked in ConPTY's WriteFile\\n- **gui:** drop 14 dead\\\\_code expectations no foreign cell fulfils\\n- **gui, session, pty:** the review of ATERM-KI-1014-6\\n- **grid:** normalize offload geometry before planning\\n- **agent:** require the restart intent before signalling\\n- **vitals:** age each trend from its last valid reading\\n- **supervise:** every turn and every loop reads a done row less the machine's sleep inside it\\n- **supervise:** a placed sleep is wholly insid