nt's tab-menu Stop is the signal verb's act, with no card (design S7, §1)\\n- **overview:** the card says what t and ⌫ do for the person reading it, and counts held workers (design S6)\\n- agents menu: Hand Back's tip says only the person's hold lifts; the live-bits slot exists only with a native menu (design S5, S7)\\n- person hold: hwkey cannot press a card's rows, and a script's tab-menu chord opens none under a hold (design S5)\\n- connected spawn: no menu caller is left, so its `surface` and the menu's first-use notice go (design S12)\\n- person hold: a standing long hold's entry says its refusals, manager and other holds as they move (design S5)\\n- person hold: a crash is not a Hand Back, and an update restarts the 30 minutes, said where they are read (design S5)\\n- status item: the local glance replaces the operator glance (S4)\\n- desktop notices default on, needs only (S4)\\n- SPECS and comments follow the S4 status item\\n- status item: the held section states the app-verb halt (S4)\\n- status item: the fleet glance (S10)\\n- status item: an open menu's clicks resolve against the glance it was painted from\\n- fleet glance: dial a peer by the name the book knows it by\\n- fleet glance: a standing need is one notice across a stale read or a silent Mac\\n- status item: a sibling's needs count only from a young scan, on a cadence\\n- status item: the red title keeps the bar's font; review minors\\n- status item: Notify Me says whose banner a notice arrives as\\n- status item: a read it opens raises its window\\n- desktop notices default on only where the banner is aterm's own\\n- status item: a seamless update carries what the owner was told and has seen\\n- status item: the review's minors — order, labels, ages, the issuer line, docs\\n- **comment:** the notice switch's boot line reads as one sentence\\n- status item: the Linux and Windows cells build again\\n- status item: Go and a raise land on the needy pane, not beside it\\n- desktop notices: on by default, needs only, as the lead ruled\\n- status item: a carried told need is adopted by its word, not its kind\\n- fleet glance: a content peer's need says what it is; a freeze dates only an agent\\n- fleet glance: a seamless update carries the fleet needs the herald told\\n- status item: a To look at line raises the window it opens Messages in\\n- status item: the hold line names sudo's password sheet; two doc fixes\\n- **fleet:** the issuer serves its book of peers, so a member's survey --fleet reads the whole fleet\\n- fleet live lane: a member's survey --fleet reaches a member only the issuer's book names\\n- fleet book: the copy in a file of its own, members read before the issuer's survey, only the issuer's refusal counts\\n- fleet live lane: the book over the real listeners, and the copy in its own file\\n- fleet book: a test for the deadline of its own past the first AT\\\\_ONCE dials\\n- fleet book: the issuer is surveyed where its book answered, a book the deadline cut short is its row, and a member never reads itself\\n- fleet peers: a person's \\\\[\\\\[fleet.peers\\\\]\\\\] entry stands for a copy at its place, and the survey's closing line is tested\\n- aterm ctl survey: the read is a pure read\\\\_survey, and the fleet client's closing line is tested\\n- fleet live lane: the book's member is read at the longest --timeout, apart from the silent port\\n- fleet issuer: a lost node id names the remedy that works, on the issuer\\n- fleet book: the issuer is surveyed where a failed book proved itself, and the seat's rule has no clock\\n- fleet read: the line short of the issuer's book says whether a copy was read\\n- fleet tests: leave's removal of the issuer-book copy is checked on a member that holds one\\n- fleet live lane: the book's reach is read in process under the hang detector, and the CLI read's budget is stated\\n- **team:** a manager's workers are listed in the order they were made\\n- owner surfaces: the fold's last cross-track stubs are wired, each with a test\\n- **menu:** a test binary keeps each published menu bit per thread; MENU\\\\_STATICS goes\\n- **cleanup:** the retired band and operator election leave docs and samples; an unconfirmed needs-switch save fits the title rule\\n- owner surfaces S12: the connection card and the drag-to-connect gesture go\\n- owner surfaces S13: teach the needs, Take Over and the opt-in; one CHANGELOG entry per change\\n- status item: Hand Back All builds for its test off macOS too\\n- **SPECS:** the herald row says what a notice with alerts off does, not a ⚠ title\\n- owner surfaces: the You hold row says what the hold refused; one cost sentence\\n- owner surfaces: one name for a local session on every surface\\n- owner surfaces: Next That Needs You walks the needs in ❯'s order\\n- owner surfaces: the Overview's title counts another aterm's sessions\\n- owner surfaces: a stall's need says the person's words, not an agent's command\\n- owner surfaces: a press on a tab's marks selects the tab\\n- owner surfaces: say notices are off until Notify Me, and drop deleted surfaces from comments\\n- **aterm-gui:** the merge's two crossed intents meet in one body\\n- **aterm-gui:** the linux-arm cell compiles clean with the status item and Team chip\\n- **aterm-gui:** the Team chip's manager mark passes as itself (tippy)\\n- **aterm-gui:** the needs border keeps a test of the idle law\\n- **presence:** a background codex that finished its turn wears the tab's done dot\\n- **aterm-gui-fabric:** the Autopilot menu does not open under a hold\\n- **aterm-gui:** the Team chip is a node of the accessibility tree\\n- **aterm-gui:** the Agents namer keeps the person's title whole\\n- **aterm-gui:** `controls overview` says task\\\\_state= for the worker's task\\n- **aterm-gui:** main's test prunes and dead-code deletions stand\\n- **aterm-gui:** set\\\\_tab\\\\_strip\\\\_rows' StripRise anchor takes main's form\\n- **presence:** a tab named only by its number is named once on the pill\\n- **messages:** the API outage's count is shown as tabs join it\\n- **aterm-gui:** a worker's line follows its starter's terminal before the sweep names it\\n- **aterm-gui:** Hand Back lifts a client's hold where no person's stands\\n- **aterm-gui:** a need's words say what to do when its pill offers no act\\n- **aterm-gui:** the operator family and the band's doc comments go\\n- **render(windows):** Claude Code's spinner keeps one weight at 200%, its ✻ untouched\\n- **aterm-pty:** a spawned shell runs in the UI tier, not the squashed legacy band\\n- **aterm-gui:** a tab's fork waits for the park at the fork; the spare gate counts no orphan an older launcher left\\n- **aterm-update:** the stage holds its start probe at the exec while the gate runs\\n- **aterm-uds:** a child started stopped dies unrun with its holder, SIGHUP at its default\\n- **aterm-update:** a refused stage kills its held probe before it removes the bundle\\n- **aterm-uds:** start\\\\_suspended says the first-exec assessment runs while the child is stopped\\n- **aterm-uds:** the control-dir test expects a Linux desktop's own runtime folder as the person's\\n- Muse Code gets the live upgrade's quiet flow\\n- lab muse-upgrade: resolve the swapped current link, report the held looks\\n- Muse quiet upgrade: the review's fixes, each guard pinned by a test\\n- Muse quiet upgrade: the final live run on the merged code, and a comment reflowed\\n- Muse quiet upgrade: the activation wake's per-agent wiring and a new worker's count, each pinned by a test\\n- **aterm-gui:** the spare gate reads the shell's pid version the moment its spawn returns\\n- aterm tests: L7's spare checks print the metrics line with them\\n- **aterm-gui:** the shell-version read says how far ahead of the rc it is\\n- **trust:** raise 6 foundational crates past 100+ proved (+692 proved) & sync astream 532fbeb\\n- **aterm:** cold start — the session-0 spawn's kit, the word lexicon and the script address leave the boot's path; chained fixups\\n- aterm-shell-integration SPECS: the address's hash half is FNV-1a/64 now\\n- aterm build.rs: the Windows banner's doc comment goes back on report\\n- **aterm-gui:** session 0's provision is made ahead on an update relaunch that withholds -e\\n- **aterm:** the start-up entry quotes both measurement runs; shell\\\\_body names the folder hash\\n- **aterm-shell-integration:** a running command's title is its whole line, and the tab end-cuts a title the shell cut\\n- **aterm-shell-integration:** bash repairs the tty after a command that ran a second, whatever its status\\n- **LAG-9:** fish's start record costs nothing measurable (sweep #11)\\n- **aterm-shell-integration:** the fish script says it needs fish 3.4, as it does\\n- **aterm-shell-integration:** a live test shell let go of is killed and reaped\\n- **atpkg:** a waiting pending stub wakes on Linux (inotify) and Windows (change notification)\\n- aterm-render on the Linux lane: the emoji gate poses its case, and the suite is green\\n- Raise Trust floors past 100 proved on 8 crates and sync vendor/astream (983a836)\\n- **aterm-render:** vf\\\\_bold\\\\_gid\\\\_raster's doc names its Linux caller\\n- **atpkg:** a waiting stub takes its inotify watches off before it execs or exits\\n- Keep saved DEBUG traps until their owning session discards them\\n- **trust:** raise 9 more crate floors above 100 proved obligations (+1149 proved)\\n- Release shader warm waiters when either lane fails\\n- Keep Fish on visible cold startup until all startup files are tracked\\n- Refuse oversized complete fleet replies before parsing success\\n- Require a written restart claim before signaling Muse\\n- **aterm-gui:** the tray's East Asian face store is CJK\\\\_STORE, so the lazy-init census sees no self-reentry\\n- Fence worker startup input against the live prompt and person takeover\\n- Bound outstanding fleet resolver work across the process\\n- Keep worker task-file cancellation sticky across the spawner\\n- **trust:** raise 10 more crate floors above 100 proved obligations (+1134 proved)\\n- **aterm-gui:** the spare backstop classifies WorkerLaunch, so aterm-gui builds again\\n- Order tab-input replay by its fresh booking identity\\n- Bound CLI child output collection after direct-child exit\\n- Return from interrupted child polls once their deadline expires\\n- **trust:** raise 10 more crate floors above 100 proved obligations (+1057 proved)\\n- aterm-gui tests on Linux: six reds on the lane pass, each for the platform reason it failed\\n- **fabric:** \\\\[fabric\\\\] command may be an argv array, so the dev app's spaced path runs the bus\\n- **fabric:** `on` never writes an argv array; a spaced aterm path runs through a link in the root\\n- **find:** keep cell geometry when routed advances break bounded scans\\n- windows control auth: the owner check is proved across an elevation on SDDL descriptors, with no UAC\\n- aterm tests: the survey's stopped-agent leg runs where aterm can read queued input\\n- gui,machines: discover Bonjour LAN computers in Tab Control Panel and aterm machines tabs\\n- Sync vendor/astream (8603b58) and eliminate 34 unproved obligations (+388 proved) across 11 crates\\n- **aterm-gui:** the story overlap test tells main's one told word (land, 5B-6, T17)\\n- **aterm-gui:** a task mark's log wake posts no need verdict (land, 5C-3, T21)\\n- aterm-gui-timing, aterm-observe: the proved byte helpers expect clippy's argument count (land)\\n- aterm-cli, aterm-gui: aterm help says where a self-claim act mark lands (land, 5C-2, T24, T38)\\n- **aterm-gui:** the help test checks the limiter's numbers, not its sentences (land, 5A-2, T38)\\n- **aterm-gui:** a test guards the task mark's split of waiter wake and need verdict (land, 5C-3, T21)\\n- **aterm-census:** slog-inert names the PTY writers' twins and fails on a dead needle (land; phase 3A ruling R5, design §7.4)\\n- **aterm-census:** pin slog-inert's dead-needle check skipping \\\\*\\\\_tests.rs files (land; phase 3A ruling R5, design §7.4)\\n- **machines:** the LAN daemon answers a beacon and nothing else; launchd no longer loops on it\\n- **machines:** no LAN daemon; follow a moved IP to its .local name, retire the old LaunchAgent\\n- **aterm-window:** recorded.rs as its crate's rustfmt.toml formats it\\n- **machines:** retiring the old LaunchAgent takes only what the job made, and starts nothing\\n- **trust:** bump vendor/astream and eliminate 60 unproved obligations across 9 crates (+96 proved)\\n- docs+test(supervise): a transcript limit row that names no reset holds the host's steps until the conversation moves (ATERM-KI-1016-1 limits-2)\\n- docs+test(supervise): a restart's lease refuses the supervisor's limit-menu press too, retried (ATERM-KI-1016-1 limits-4)\\n- docs+test(supervise): a bucket notice nothing dates is read by the fallback's latch alone (ATERM-KI-1016-1 limits-6)\\n- docs+test(manual): a person's prompt moves a limit row's hold only once the model answers it (ATERM-KI-1016-1 limits-2)\\n- turn end: a draft over a menu the screen cannot read is told once, never pressed (screens-2)\\n- **approval:** the Edit tool's own box is the levels' where the screen and the transcript both name its call (screens-3)\\n- box head: a box taller than the pane is held, the owner told, wherever its head is not read whole within 400 rows (screens-1)\\n- **approval:** the Edit tool's box is its message's queued run's top, past the agent's text (screens-3 review)\\n- **manual:** the boxes paragraph's tall-box sentence rewrapped to the page (screens-1 review)\\n- **decide(harness):** an agent the upgrade ended is said down in a tab Off set aside (lifecycle-1)\\n- **decide(harness):** a driver's writes under its lease are no person's keys; what it left holds the line (lifecycle-2, LC-7)\\n- **decide(restore):** a held tab reopens held, its agent the holder's; a lift no image carries comes back (lifecycle-3, LC-8)\\n- **manual:** two lines the done and limits lanes added rewrapped to their paragraphs' width\\n- **aterm-gui:** session 0's shell is forked before the event loop is built\\n- **aterm-shell-integration:** the script folder is named with FxHasher, not FNV-1a/64\\n- **aterm-gui:** session\\\\_log's attribution tests are unix tests, as their handles are\\n- **aterm-update-core:** a silently dead download is given up in \\\\~14 s and continued in-call\\n- **aterm-update-core:** a link that keeps moving is continued past sixteen hiccups; bytes already at download\\\\_to's dest are never continued\\n- **aterm-update-core:** a resumable attempt probes an idle connection every 2 s, not 5\\n- **atpkg:** a release row naming the dmg lane is refused as an https one is\\n- **atpkg:** the dmg lane's post-copy vet refusal is tested through the stage\\n- **aterm-agent:** a probe run counts a hundred steps, not three hundred\\n- LAG-11 review: say why the script folder may persist an FxHasher name, and quote the idle band\\n- **LAG-12:** no work interval for the idle slow clock (warm-spare design D6)\\n- **spare:** fish tabs get their warm spare back over the startup roots fish reports (R7)\\n- **spare:** the generation stamps path\\\\_helper's PATH list and fish's themes folder\\n- **vendor(astream):** advance submodule to 72a46fb (+702 proved / -74 unknown in astream, unlock BrokerLog on drop)\\n- **LAG-12:** D6 carries the four-round result: the interval made the shell's first prompt later\\n- LAG-12 review: D6 measured in aterm.app's own coalition too\\n- **aterm-gui:** a stream that stalls under a frame keeps its output holds\\n- **aterm-gui:** say why a stream's quiet window is one frame, and whose 0.38 ms\\n- **grid:** a shrink under owed pushed rows pushes the blank row a push left, never trims it (S2R-F4 corner b)\\n- **grid:** a width change lays the rows out where the hand-back puts them (S2R-F4 corner a)\\n- cast drift: each recording replays under the resize law its header names (S2R-F4 corner c)\\n- **aterm-slog:** the instance's node log (5J-1)\\n- aterm-gui, aterm-gui-fabric: start, link and config records (5J-2)\\n- aterm-gui, aterm-types: log n reads the node log (5J-3)\\n- **aterm-gui:** await log takes a list of predicates (5F-1)\\n- aterm-agent, aterm-gui: the hosted lanes say they relaunched (5F-2)\\n- **aterm-slog:** a turn's close restates its ledger= (5F-4a)\\n- **aterm-agent:** drive ledger --source log, beside the old path (5F-4)\\n- **aterm-ctl:** survey --brief, the local brief (5F-6)\\n- **aterm-ctl:** the survey walk dials one instance at a time (5F-6)\\n- **aterm-lab:** lab reduce, a key-only reducer (5H-1)\\n- **aterm-agent:** measured builds are a committed set (5H-2a)\\n- **aterm-agent:** a lab-read reduction makes its build exact (5H-2b)\\n- **aterm-gui:** the transcript apply's hold is a metric (5H-3)\\n- **aterm-gui:** a read with no new rows books its one hold (5H-3)\\n- **aterm-lab:** format the reducer's dead-code expectation (5H-1)\\n- **aterm-ctl:** a since-less await log list is asked again only when all need (5F-1)\\n- **aterm-ctl:** survey --brief briefs an instance that refuses log n (5F-6)\\n- **aterm-agent:** drive ledger --source log names a turn no exchange opened (5F-4)\\n- **aterm-lab:** lab reduce keeps no key or stamp tail anyone wrote (5H-1)\\n- **aterm-lab:** lab reduce frees every place a tool's names sit (5H-1)\\n- **aterm-lab:** lab reduce frees a call's second input copy and every tool schema (5H-1)\\n- aterm-core SPECS: the flap identity holds through the bottom-push and rewrap corners\\n- cast drift: name the law test's corner tuple (tippy type\\\\_complexity)\\n- **shell-integration:** an in-place upgrade takes off the old \\\\~/.aterm/bin entry\\n- **codesign:** a dangling symlink and a later-line fault stay verdicts\\n- **update:** codesign's own progress lines and a quoted refusal key never make a verdict pass (r8 #37, review)\\n- **aterm-update:** no decision reads floor/failed/quarantine ledgers permissively\\n- **update:** judge the appcast sig after the roster observation; one filing per stage state across the park\\n- **update:** a codesign refusal is a moment only on the verified path's own line; ditto's words are quoted (r8 #37, third review)\\n- **update:** gates read quarantine records strictly; codesign never waits on a FIFO; test the yank and authority call sites\\n- **trust:** raise aterm-agent's floor to 4509/25102 and correct aterm-cli's total to 1005\\n- **aterm-gui:** Settings' rail grows to its widest name in the face it is drawn in\\n- **aterm-gui:** crash-journal tests date their panic reports after the run armed\\n- Linux lane: web2, the worktree's git, Trust's absence and Rosetta's limits decided\\n- aterm-objc tests: the SDK declaration parser passes over a `pub const fn`\\n- **aterm-gui:** the rail test judges 1.25x, where full names overran it first\\n- **vendor(astream):** bump to 4db9781 (+229 proved / -194 unknown obligations in astream-broker)\\n- resize hand-back: a line's head comes onto the screen before a width change; pushes cut seams, never splice\\n- resize hand-back: the window's top is a cell, so a zoom flap over a line the screen's top cuts comes back\\n- **update:** the day-long digest line names no platform (ATERM-KI-1015-2)\\n- **manual:** Linux update checks wait while a build is on trial, as the product's rule (ATERM-KI-1015-2)\\n- **input:** an xkb chord under Caps Lock takes Shift's capital (ATERM-KI-1015-9, the X11/Wayland case)\\n- **style(gui):** trustfmt the xkb chord test and the fork-lane descriptor test\\n- The parent installs an update before LaunchServices launches its successor, so that successor never re-execs\\n- Review fixes for the parent-swaps-first handoff: withdraw a dead successor's stale-record entry, and correct the lane prose\\n- A fresh window ends the stale-record entry, and the last premises say who swaps\\n- Every window measures its own LaunchServices record and says when it is stale\\n- **spec(gui):** mh-health-latch-heal names the queued owed row's patience restart (ATERM-KI-1015-2, U37 review)\\n- **aterm-gui:** the toolbar drive's state count is the groups' own\\n- **aterm-gui:** objc\\\\_ime\\\\_drive's Option-as-Alt stage gets a control that composes\\n- **aterm-gui:** the toolbar drive reads a click made without activation as not measured\\n- **aterm-verify:** the objc exit contract names both weaker passes and the toolbar's activation 2\\n- **aterm-gui:** objc\\\\_ime\\\\_drive judges only the key it sends\\n- **aterm-window:** replace\\\\_event's doc cites the dead-key measurement\\n- **primer:** drop ATERM-TASK-DONE from the CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md section (v28)\\n- harness card: a cuter kitty, and the rainbow meets its haunch\\n- harness card: the border stands in the card's air\\n- **claude\\\\_footer:** read a new Claude Code's registry row on a 100 ms ladder, so the harness card is decorated at load\\n- harness card: the resolver's pass is tested as run calls it, the two-row kitty's mouth stands on its chin, and the docs say what was measured\\n- **claude\\\\_card:** the air comment names agy's four-row card\\n- **aterm-gui:** main builds again after …\\n- aterm-core, aterm-render, aterm-gpu: tippy passes again after …\\n- aterm-lab, aterm-agent: the lab's Codex 0.163.0 rollouts, reduced (5G lab run; T9, T33)\\n- **aterm-phase:** Codex's rollout keys, from a committed rollout (5G-1; T9)\\n- **aterm-agent:** a Codex rollout step fold (5G-2; T9, T33, S6)\\n- A macOS window launch keeps its image and leaves a ready update for its own window\\n- Window launch keeps its image: press-only never escapes, one boot router, waits said true\\n- Window launch keeps its image: the bar waits for a terminal too, recheck fixes\\n- Recheck lab instance custody after crash preparation waits\\n- Preserve post-shell PATH directories with backdated modification times\\n- **aterm-gui:** the warm spare on Linux, both tiers, with a /proc escape scan\\n- **aterm-gui:** the Linux scan's tick rate reads c\\\\_ulong as the codebase does on LP64\\n- **aterm-gui:** the Linux scan declares getauxval itself, so x86\\\\_64 Linux builds\\n- **aterm\\\\_suite:** the turn-submit stand-in draws its draft when the Enter comes with it\\n- **aterm-gui:** the Linux scan judges a live thread group whose leader exited, and a parked spawn looks for the system files again\\n- **aterm-gui:** rewrap the /proc stat parser's doc comment\\n- Share the argv0 alias list and deny the amacs editor hint per hop\\n- Name build.ps1's prose alias lists and drop a repeated EDITOR assert\\n- Harden account source curl configuration and protocols\\n- Preserve unknown Linux proc reads before warm promotion\\n\\n_Truncated to fit GitHub's release-body limit — the complete note is `release-notes/v0.107.0.md` in this release's source tree._\\n\\n---\\n\\nSource release. `SHA256SUMS` is a per-file manifest of the released tree, with a detached Ed25519 signature (`SHA256SUMS.sig`) by a machine key named in the attached master-signed roster (`aterm-machines.toml` + `.sig`). Verification chain and key inventory: SIGNING.md in the publication engine; the roster pin is committed in aterm `crates/aterm-update-core/src/pins.rs`.\\n"}
